      content: ["EduAIR, in collaboration with the CUHK Jockey Club AI for the Future Project, jointly hosted a booth at the Learning and Teaching Expo 2024, held from 11 - 13 December, 2024. The booth featured our self-developed artificial intelligence (AI) teaching toolkits, including iCar and iPort, and providing an interactive platform for visitors to explore and engage with cutting-edge AI technology.", "The booth showcased a range of innovative applications, such as an image-controlled iPort car racing arena and various educational experiments utilizing iCar and iPort. These included iCar moral dilemma, face following, and line tracking demonstrations. The exhibits emphasized the practical integration of AI into teaching and learning scenarios. Furthermore, interactive AI displays highlighted the adaptability of iPort in connecting with various hardware devices and its integration with EduAIR's iTrain online AI model training platform. Key exhibits included the AI Teddy Bear and the AI Rock-Paper-Scissors. Participants enthusiastically engaged in hands-on activities, gaining a foundational understanding of AI principles through block-based programming.", "Through illustrating how AI technology can be effectively leveraged to enhance teaching methodologies, this event aimed to inspire the education sector to cultivate creativity and innovation in instructional practices, and provide valuable insights and support for the development of future teaching and learning models."],
