      subtitle: "",
      location: "G/F Special Exhibition Hall, Hong Kong Science Museum",
      content: ["To celebrate the 75th anniversary of the founding of the People's Republic of China, the Leisure and Cultural Services Department (LCSD) launched the \"Glorious Voyage: Splendid Achievements of the People's Republic of China in Its 75 Years\" Exhibition Series, at the Hong Kong Science Museum (HKScM) , EduAIR was honored to showcase our developed artificial intelligence (AI) exhibits at the \"Era of Intelligence\" exhibition, including \"Master Guess\", \"Smart Oil Painting\" and \"iPort Car\". \"Master Guess\" allows visitors to provide hand gestures data for \"rock\", \"paper\" and \"scissors\" to an AI model and compete against a robotic hand. \"Smart Oil Painting\" changes the style of paintings through deep learning and then uses robotic automation technology to draw the artworks with brushes. \"iPort Car\" allows visitors to experience controlling a car with hand gestures to complete tasks, showcasing AI teaching experiments conducted using iPort. This exhibition aims to demonstrate the wide applications of AI to the public and provide hands-on experiences through interactive exhibits, hoping to spark the audience's interest in AI."],
