      content: ["The six-week \"Work Shadowing Program\" has successfully concluded, and the graduation ceremony was attended by EduAIR board members, Professor Yan Nang from the Department of Mechanical and Automation Engineering at CUHK, as well as several parents and teachers, who witnessed the students' impressive achievements.", "This program invited outstanding students from the \"AI Quiz Competition for Secondary School Students 2025\" to personally participate in research projects at CUHK during the summer, allowing them to gain firsthand experience in the real world of engineering and innovation. They also had the opportunity to participate in patent applications, turning their ideas into actual inventions. After six weeks of hard work, the participating students successfully designed and created a paint mixing machine, showcasing their comprehensive application of engineering learning. This machine not only exemplifies the practical application of interdisciplinary knowledge but also highlights the students' creativity and teamwork spirit."],
