    layout: "default",
    "en": {
      title: "Professional Development Workshop on the Application of AI in Teaching and Learning",
      subtitle: "",
      location: "Heep Yunn Primary School",
      content: ["To enhance teachers’ knowledge and skills in applying AI in education, Heep Yunn Primary School organized a professional development workshop titled “The Application of AI in Teaching and Learning” on November 11, 2025. The school invited the EduAIR team as guest speakers to lead the workshop. Focusing on the practical use of generative AI tools in real classroom settings, the event attracted the enthusiastic participation of over 50 educators, reflecting the staff’s strong commitment to embracing digital transformation in education.", "The workshop introduced a range of cutting-edge AI platforms, including Gamma, Napkin.AI, Canva, the POE platform, and Brisk Teaching. Through hands -on practice and live demonstrations, teachers were guided on how to utilize the unique features of each platform to enhance teaching strategies and classroom design. In the Brisk Teaching session, participants explored how to quickly adjust the level of lesson content based on student abilities and design differentiated instruction using the platform’s built -in tools. Interactive tasks and real-time feedback mechanisms were also highlighted as effective means to boost student engagement and participation—further reinforcing a student- centered approach to teaching.", "In terms of lesson planning and delivery, teachers learned to use the Gamma platform to efficiently generate well-structured and visually appealing teaching slides, improving both preparation efficiency and instructional quality. Napkin.AI was introduced as a tool to convert abstract or complex concepts into clear diagrams and flowcharts, enhancing students' comprehension and knowledge organizat ion. Meanwhile, Canva was showcased for its capabilities in designing interactive and gamified learning activities that enrich classroom dynamics and motivate student learning.", "The workshop also featured a focused session on Prompt Engineering, equipping teachers with the skills to craft precise and purposeful prompts that improve the responsiveness and educational relevance of AI tools. The POE platform was another highlight, wi th teachers engaging in hands-on exercises to build personalized AI teaching assistants that support lesson planning, question generation, and differentiated learning. This practical experience further demonstrated the diverse ways AI can serve as a powerf ul support tool in modern teaching.", "Overall, the workshop was both insightful and highly practical. Participants expressed that it not only deepened their understanding of generative AI technologies but also inspired new ideas for creative and effective teaching practices."],
    },
