      title: "Professional Development Workshop on the Application of AI in Teaching and Learning",
      subtitle: "",
      location: "Yan Chai Hospital Choi Hin To Primary School",
      content: ["To support teachers in enhancing their ability to utilize digital tools in education, Yan Chai Hospital Choi Hin To Primary School successfully hosted the \"AI in Teaching and Learning Applications\" workshop on December 12, 2025, in collaboration with the EduAIR team. Focused on hands-on practice and case studies, the workshop guided teachers in exploring new models of digital teaching, optimizing lesson planning and classroom engagement strategies, and ultimately improving teaching effectiveness and student participation.", "The workshop featured several practical themes. Teachers started with training on the Brisk Teaching tool, learning how to adjust lesson difficulty to better meet the diverse needs of their students while utilizing interactive features to boost student engagement and focus. In the \"Precision Teaching Design\" session, teachers developed skills to craft clear and structured lesson plans, improving the quality and relevance of their teaching content.", "The workshop also highlighted the practical applications of Gamma and Napkin tools for lesson design. Teachers gained hands-on experience creating organized and visually appealing presentations and teaching flowcharts, enabling them to communicate lesson content more effectively and enhance learning outcomes through concise visual design. Meanwhile, through the POE platform exercise, teachers explored how to develop personalized teaching assistants to support lesson planning, create guiding questions, and aid individualized learning, further enhancing teaching flexibility and support for students.", "Additionally, the workshop emphasized the integration of creativity and interaction. Using the Canva platform, teachers learned how to incorporate gamified elements into classroom activities, designing engaging and participatory learning experiences. This approach allowed students to explore knowledge in a lively and interactive environment, fostering their curiosity, interest, and motivation to learn."],
