      subtitle: "",
      location: "Fanling Public School",
      content: ["To embrace the rapid transformation of education through technology, Fanling Public School partnered with EduAIR to successfully host the \"AI Applications in Teaching and Learning\" Professional Training Workshop on January 3, 2026. This event aimed to equip teachers with practical methods for incorporating generative AI tools into their teaching practices. Through a combination of hands-on activities and application-driven training, the workshop guided teachers in exploring innovative digital teaching models, refining lesson preparation workflows, and revolutionizing classroom engagement strategies.", "The workshop was carefully designed to address the practical challenges and needs of modern classrooms. Teachers learned how to implement differentiated instruction through tools like Brisk Teaching, which allowed them to rapidly adjust lesson difficulty to meet the diverse needs of their students. By incorporating interactive generative tasks, the training also demonstrated how teachers could foster a more engaging and participatory classroom atmosphere. A strong emphasis was placed on human-AI collaboration, with teachers developing essential skills in crafting effective instructional prompts. In addition, the workshop examined how intelligent tools such as Gamma and Napkin AI could transform complex teaching concepts into clear, well-structured, and visually appealing presentations. The workshop further introduced forward-thinking approaches by teaching participants how to build their own personalized AI teaching assistants using the POE platform. Moreover, teachers explored ways to integrate Canva's creative design features with coding elements, enabling them to gamify learning processes and spark students' curiosity and motivation."],
