      subtitle: "",
      location: "Shun Tak Fraternal Association Leung Kau Kui College",
      content: ["The EduAIR team was honored to be invited on January 6, 2026, to visit Shun Tak Fraternal Association Leung Kau Kui College, where they conducted a professional training workshop themed \"AI in Teaching and Learning Applications.\" The workshop aimed to enhance teachers' ability to integrate generative AI tools into their classroom practices. The event fostered an engaging and lively learning environment as teachers wholeheartedly participated, actively exchanged ideas, and demonstrated a keen interest in innovating their teaching methods with AI technologies.", "The introductory section of the workshop focused on the practical applications of key AI tools. Teachers explored the POE platform to generate teaching outlines and personalized AI chatbots, used Gamma to create visually structured and concise teaching presentations, and utilized Napkin.AI to convert texts into flowcharts and logic diagrams, making abstract concepts easier to teach and understand. Additionally, the instructors provided an in-depth explanation of Prompt Engineering techniques, equipping teachers with the skills to create precise and effective prompts, significantly improving the efficiency and usability of generative AI tools.", "In the lesson example-sharing session, the instructors showcased innovative applications of AI in various subjects. In language classes, teachers learned how to transform text into visual imagery, enhancing students' comprehension of reading materials. In math and science classes, educators used tools like Canva to design 3D models and animated simulations, offering students a more intuitive grasp of geometric and physical concepts. Moreover, teachers had hands-on experience developing engaging and interactive classroom activities using Canva, further sparking student interest and promoting active participation. Through a combination of hands-on tool training and practical case studies, the workshop enabled teachers to master the core operations and instructional strategies of generative AI, boosting their confidence and proficiency while inspiring innovative thinking about classroom design and reshaping teaching practices."],
