      subtitle: "On-Campus Workshop at CCC Ming Kei College",
      location: "CCC Ming Kei College",
      content: ["From January 22 to January 30, 2026, the EduAIR team hosted a four-session iPort Intelligent Technology Workshop at CCC Ming Kei College for secondary two and three students. The workshop aimed to enhance students' understanding and practical application of intelligent technologies by combining theoretical learning with hands-on experience, encouraging them to explore the possibilities of technological innovation.", "The workshop focused on fundamental applications of intelligent technology. Students utilized the iPort platform to complete a range of experiments and create practical applications, including designing a system capable of identifying strangers and triggering an alarm, as well as building a voice-controlled lighting system. Additionally, students assembled iPort smart wooden vehicles, trained the system to enable the vehicles to respond to different colored signs with corresponding movements, and participated in a resource competition to showcase their innovation skills and experimental outcomes.", "The course emphasized the development of practical skills and problem-solving abilities, integrating competitive elements to effectively spark students' curiosity and interest in learning. It introduced students to the basic concepts and principles of intelligent technologies, aiming to help them build a solid understanding of modern technologies, improve critical thinking and hands-on capabilities, and inspire enthusiasm for further exploration in the field."],
