      subtitle: "",
      location: "Fung Kai No. 1 Secondary School",
      content: ["To support teachers in mastering the use of digital tools in education, Fung Kai No. 1 Secondary School successfully hosted the \"AI in Teaching and Learning Applications\" workshop on January 29, 2026, in collaboration with the EduAIR team for the planning and design of the event. Centered around hands-on practice, the workshop explored strategies ranging from instructional design to classroom interactions, showcasing how digital technologies can effectively enhance educational practices. Teachers participated enthusiastically, and the workshop was met with great acclaim.", "The workshop focused on innovative teaching strategies and platform applications, including the practical use of the Brisk Teaching tool. Teachers experienced how to adapt teaching materials to meet the diverse needs of students and effectively use interactive modules to boost classroom engagement, thereby improving students' focus and learning efficiency. Additionally, during the \"Precision Teaching Design\" session, teachers mastered techniques for crafting effective prompts, enabling them to optimize instructional activities and resources with greater accuracy.", "The workshop also highlighted the practical applications of Gamma and Napkin teaching design tools. Participants learned how to quickly create well-structured and visually engaging presentations and flowcharts, enhancing lesson planning and ensuring that educational content was presented in a clear and accessible way. Furthermore, teachers explored the functionalities of the POE platform, where they experimented with creating personalized digital assistants to streamline lesson preparation, generate guided questions, and support individualized student learning needs.", "Lastly, the workshop emphasized combining creative design elements with the Canva platform, helping teachers incorporate gamified and interactive features into lesson plans. This approach effectively sparked students' interest and motivation, delivering a vibrant and diverse classroom experience. The workshop was packed with enriching and practical content, tailored to educators' real-world needs. Through hands-on training and case studies, teachers not only gained confidence in using digital tools but also broadened their perspectives on classroom innovation and educational transformation."],
