      subtitle: "",
      location: "Fuzhou Strait International Conference and Exhibition Center",
      content: ["The EduAIR team was honoured to be invited to Fuzhou to participate in the 9th Digital China Summit, held at the Fuzhou Strait International Conference and Exhibition Center. EduAIR exhibited at the \"Hong Kong Pavilion\", jointly organised by the Digital Policy Office and the Fujian Liaison Unit of the Government of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region.", "The Hong Kong Pavilion showcased a wide range of innovation and technology achievements from Hong Kong. During the event, EduAIR showcased the iPort and iTrain AI education platforms developed by The Chinese University of Hong Kong team, demonstrating how AI learning can be brought into school classrooms in an accessible and practical manner.", "One of the key interactive exhibits, \"Rock-Paper-Scissors Master\", attracted many visitors to participate in hands-on demonstrations. The exhibit vividly demonstrated how AI can be applied in image recognition, pattern analysis, and real-time decision-making.", "EduAIR believes that AI education is not only about acquiring technological knowledge, but also about nurturing students' creativity, problem-solving skills, digital literacy, and future readiness. Moving forward, EduAIR will continue to promote the integration of AI education into mainstream classrooms."],
